      "url": "https://thestrollingbones.blogspot.com/2026/09/go-west-young-man.html",
      "title": "[Kagi Small Web] Go West Young Man",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=kagi.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=kagi.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=kagi.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=kagi.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=kagi.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\nThe forecast for the whole week was dry and sunny, with light winds, so I headed off in the camper for a week in Dorset. Bully arranged to meet me there, so he was free to load up his car with even more ridiculous amounts of gear than normal. We found a nice campsite on Portland. Quiet, great views, with a fifteen minute walk to the rocks. Light rods and float gear was the order of the day and on the first afternoon we had lots of ballan and corking wrasse, with the occasional pollack. Nothing big but a bit",
